  "base_commit": "4c0b2ac0becfc465e63013d9b73334f3697e47f7",
  "scope": "Lucky Stars scene state constants, dealer counter and card animation names, local variables and corrected comments.",
  "changes": [
    "Name the fourteen scene states in a class enum and use those names for existing explicit state assignments and comparisons. Keep the integer state storage and sequential increments.",
    "Rename mDealCount to mCardsDealt and mRevealStep to mRevealTick. Clarify card selection, position traversal, arrival counts, score/credits, input and palette locals.",
    "Correct the header description of vertical card movement and the source description of the dealer counter. Remove obsolete claims that inherited score fields are unnamed. Format implementations consistently while preserving scope, declaration and function order."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "dealer_counter": "StateDealCards clears the counter and passes its address as Dealer_StartDeal argument4. That helper stores it at shared+0x1d4, and forwards it through Dealer_StartCollect. Dealer_StateCollect increments the pointed short at animation frame5. StateWaitDeal iterates only the cards already dealt and waits for both to arrive. The shared helper source was inspected without edits.",
    "animation": "mRevealTick increments each update, resets on reaching4, then advances both card frames. Card values are chosen from five possibilities with a used-value array and forward wrapping to avoid duplicates.",
    "states": "The enum follows the fourteen pointer-to-member entries. Slots7/8 queue win/lose reactions,9/10 wait for those animations,11 returns cards,12 waits for the coin status,13 waits for the shared result flow. Slots12/13 dispatch the empty StateDone handler; CanEndState controls their transitions. No function table order or numeric value changed.",
    "coordinates": "StateMoveCards passes chosen.y and other.y to ApproachLinear with fixed-point targets0x90000 and0x30000. Both arguments are vertical; the previous header incorrectly described an x target.",
    "ownership": "Queue24 state e405c968eab0f6c2beb845907ca6d2e92c024400 has no active BSC class/file/range conflicts. Production ov006 ranges: text0x02124908..0x0212568c, init0x0213326c..0x021333e0, ctor0x021335e0..0x021335e4, bss0x02142f94..0x02143004.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator experiment required: names follow explicit accesses, state dispatch, arithmetic and the shared dealer implementation. Names are reconstructed descriptions, not recovered original identifiers.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep reverse function order and the file-wide strength-reduction pragma.",
      "Keep manual factory construction, inline destructor placement, native shared-member teardown, pointer traversal and per-iteration counter reloads.",
      "Keep integer mState storage, sequential state increments, CanEndState goto flow, volatile player-slot reads and score-pointer updates. No shared dealer implementation was edited."
    ]
  },
